---Message to be used to configure custom alerting in the {@code EventConfig} protos for an event.
---@class gcp.unstable.integrations_v1.GoogleCloudIntegrationsV1alphaIntegrationAlertConfig
---@field aggregationPeriod? string The period over which the metric value should be aggregated and evaluated. Format is , where integer should be a positive integer and unit should be one of (s,m,h,d,w) meaning (second, minute, hour, day, week). For an EXPECTED_MIN threshold, this aggregation_period must be lesser than 24 hours.
---@field thresholdType? gcp.unstable.integrations_v1.GoogleCloudIntegrationsV1alphaIntegrationAlertConfigThresholdTypeEnum|string The threshold type, whether lower(expected_min) or upper(expected_max), for which this alert is being configured. If value falls below expected_min or exceeds expected_max, an alert will be fired.
---@field displayName? string Name of the alert. This will be displayed in the alert subject. If set, this name should be unique within the scope of the integration.
---@field metricType? gcp.unstable.integrations_v1.GoogleCloudIntegrationsV1alphaIntegrationAlertConfigMetricTypeEnum|string The type of metric.
---@field disableAlert? boolean Set to false by default. When set to true, the metrics are not aggregated or pushed to Monarch for this integration alert.
---@field durationThreshold? string Should be specified only for *AVERAGE_DURATION and *PERCENTILE_DURATION metrics. This member should be used to specify what duration value the metrics should exceed for the alert to trigger.
---@field alertThreshold? number For how many contiguous aggregation periods should the expected min or max be violated for the alert to be fired.
---@field onlyFinalAttempt? boolean For either events or tasks, depending on the type of alert, count only final attempts, not retries.
---@field thresholdValue? gcp.unstable.integrations_v1.GoogleCloudIntegrationsV1alphaIntegrationAlertConfigThresholdValue The metric value, above or below which the alert should be triggered.

---@alias gcp.unstable.integrations_v1.GoogleCloudIntegrationsV1alphaIntegrationAlertConfigList gcp.unstable.integrations_v1.GoogleCloudIntegrationsV1alphaIntegrationAlertConfig[]

---@alias gcp.unstable.integrations_v1.GoogleCloudIntegrationsV1alphaIntegrationAlertConfigMetricTypeEnum "METRIC_TYPE_UNSPECIFIED"|"EVENT_ERROR_RATE"|"EVENT_WARNING_RATE"|"TASK_ERROR_RATE"|"TASK_WARNING_RATE"|"TASK_RATE"|"EVENT_RATE"|"EVENT_AVERAGE_DURATION"|"EVENT_PERCENTILE_DURATION"|"TASK_AVERAGE_DURATION"|"TASK_PERCENTILE_DURATION"

---@alias gcp.unstable.integrations_v1.GoogleCloudIntegrationsV1alphaIntegrationAlertConfigThresholdTypeEnum "THRESHOLD_TYPE_UNSPECIFIED"|"EXPECTED_MIN"|"EXPECTED_MAX"

---The threshold value of the metric, above or below which the alert should be triggered. See EventAlertConfig or TaskAlertConfig for the different alert metric types in each case. For the *RATE metrics, one or both of these fields may be set. Zero is the default value and can be left at that. For *PERCENTILE_DURATION metrics, one or both of these fields may be set, and also, the duration threshold value should be specified in the threshold_duration_ms member below. For *AVERAGE_DURATION metrics, these fields should not be set at all. A different member, threshold_duration_ms, must be set in the EventAlertConfig or the TaskAlertConfig.
---@class gcp.unstable.integrations_v1.GoogleCloudIntegrationsV1alphaIntegrationAlertConfigThresholdValue
---@field absolute? string Absolute value threshold.
---@field percentage? number Percentage threshold.

