---The response for testing an integration.
---@class gcp.unstable.integrations_v1.GoogleCloudIntegrationsV1alphaTestIntegrationsResponse
---@field hardenedPaths? gcp.unstable.integrations_v1.GoogleCloudIntegrationsV1alphaTestIntegrationsResponseHardenedPathsItemEnumList The credential paths the hardened flow covers for this test: each one that a task in the tested integration reaches and that the server running the test hardens, whatever the credential mode. A `CREDENTIAL_MODE_CURRENT` test of an integration not stored as hardened usually lists none, and a `CREDENTIAL_MODE_HARDENED` response with no paths means nothing in this integration was hardened. Empty where the hardened flow is switched off. Unset for asynchronous tests. Derived from the integration's task types before the run: it reports presence in the graph, not execution, so a task on a branch that did not run is still counted, as is a Call Integration task that runs as a configured service account. A sub-integration's own tasks are not included; each runs under its own stored disposition. Integration Connectors tasks and Cloud Scheduler triggers are never reported: the services they call do not yet accept the hardened credential.
---@field executionId? string The id of the execution corresponding to this run of integration.
---@field eventParameters? gcp.unstable.integrations_v1.EnterpriseCrmFrontendsEventbusProtoEventParameters Details for the integration that were executed.
---@field parameters? gcp.unstable.integrations_v1.GoogleCloudIntegrationsV1alphaValueTypeMap Optional. Parameters are a part of Event and can be used to communicate between different tasks that are part of the same integration execution.
---@field executionFailed? boolean Is true if any execution in the integration failed. False otherwise.
---@field parameterEntries? gcp.unstable.integrations_v1.EnterpriseCrmFrontendsEventbusProtoParameterEntryList Parameters are a part of Event and can be used to communicate between different tasks that are part of the same integration execution.
